# Targets chezmoi should delete rather than merely stop managing. Removing a
# file from the source directory only makes chezmoi forget about it; the copy
# already on disk stays and keeps being sourced.
#
# fzf's own installer generates these two, and both rc files used to source
# them. They now initialise fzf inline instead, so the leftovers are dead code
# that also appended a Homebrew keg path -- the one difference that stopped
# bash and zsh from resolving identical PATHs on macOS.
.fzf.zsh
.fzf.bash
